00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:18.150
Hanabusa-kun is battling Isabella using succès batter to make macarons.

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:26.360
So the other team is using an Italian meringue.

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:28.710
Good. Then I'll go with a French meringue.

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:32.920
Satsuki, what's the difference between an Italian meringue and a French meringue?

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:38.180
For an Italian meringue, you heat it, and it finishes very solidly.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:44.760
On the other hand for French meringue you don't heat it, and add sugar directly.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:47.470
That causes a gloss to appear when you bake it.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:48.390
I see.

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:57.650
Just as Kashino predicted, for the choux batter battle, both teams chose to make a Paris-Brest, with only the creams differing.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:06.420
So my opponent is going with a praline almond and bitter chocolate cream.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:08.890
That's a classic type.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:11.110
What kind of cream will you go with?

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:14.600
If I go head on, it'll just be a repeat of what happened with the entremet.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:18.030
Worrying doesn't become you!

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:21.260
Aneki?

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:23.850
Makoto-kun's older sister?

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:29.310
Makoto-kun's older sister? I'm Koshiro Miya!

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.420
Makoto-kun and I...

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:31.120
Out of my way.

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:34.710
Ojou-sama, are you okay?

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:35.430
Yeah...

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:39.940
Could it be? Is Makoto-kun's sister a bigger sadist than him?

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:45.280
Makoto, we've finally convinced Mother and Father to allow us to be married!

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:52.330
Is now really the time to announce this?

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:54.510
You're a Japanese man, right?

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:57.340
Stop worrying, and press forward with that Japanese spirit!

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:00.290
Japanese spirit?

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.140
Wait...

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:06.790
For the entremet, we got high marks even with the Japanese taste...

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:10.680
And there are 2 Japanese among the judges...

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:14.840
Okay then... I'm going with a Japanese style cream!

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:17.020
Thanks, Aneki!

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:20.100
Grandma...

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:25.680
I just had to go up against their leader, François, for the pie batter match!

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:30.400
Ichigo, look!

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:35.130
Look what she did to the batter... And that folding method...

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:43.410
Now that I think about it, grandma made a pie like that once...

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:49.440
The pie turned out amazingly flaky, and really delicious.

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:52.640
I won't be able to handle such a difficult folding technique.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:56.810
Instead, I need to thin out the crust and make many layers...

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.820
Amano-san, pie batter can be no thinner than 6 millimeters.

00:21:01.130 --> 00:21:02.770
If you roll it out thinner than that...

